# The image builds the Rust workspace and nothing else. The front-end sources
# (`admin/`, `studio/`, `website/`) are not needed: their `pnpm build` output is
# tracked under `crates/apiplant-assets/assets`, which is what the binary
# embeds. Neither is `examples/` — several carry a `.apiplant-build/target`
# worth hundreds of megabytes each.
#
# Written as deny-everything then allow-what-is-needed, so a new top-level
# directory stays out of the build context until someone opts it in.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates

# Build output that lives inside the allowed tree.
crates/**/target
crates/**/node_modules
